Many thanks for your comments. As described in issue #102402, actually outerVolumeSpecName is used when checking if all volumes are mounted. If innerName and outerName of an ephemeral volume are different, it will never be seen as mounted.

```
func (vm *volumeManager) getUnmountedVolumes(podName types.UniquePodName, expectedVolumes []string) []string {
	mountedVolumes := sets.NewString()
	for _, mountedVolume := range vm.actualStateOfWorld.GetMountedVolumesForPod(podName) {
		mountedVolumes.Insert(mountedVolume.OuterVolumeSpecName)
	}
	return filterUnmountedVolumes(mountedVolumes, expectedVolumes)
}
```

And yes, volumeSpec.Name() is not outerVolumeName actually, I just do an internal convension from outerName to innerName in `ConstructVolumeSpec` implemenation in our self-developed plugin, which may not implemented by other third-party storage plugins.
